    "result_text": "The change is complete and the test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `registrationDate` on the owner-create flow: when omitted, it defaults to the server's current date; when supplied it's kept, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` is `allOf` `OwnerFields`, this generates a `LocalDate registrationDate` in both `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response); Jackson serializes `LocalDate` as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `registrationDate` `LocalDate` field mapped to the `registration_date` column, with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name automatically in both directions.\n\n3. **New function `DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate`** \u2014 Sets `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when the mapped entity has none. Wired into `owners.POST.yml` as a governed step between `build` and `save` (a supplied date passes through untouched).\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added `registration_date DATE` to the owners table in all four dialects (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres). Fixed the hsqldb `data.sql` seed inserts (which used implicit column lists) by appending a `NULL` for the new column; the other dialects use explicit column lists and needed no change.\n\n**Tests:** `AcceptanceTest.coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` both pass; full `mvn test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS (2/2, 0 failures).\n\nOne note on scope: the update path (`PUT /owners/{ownerId}`, via `ApplyOwner`) does not modify `registrationDate`, so an existing owner's registration date is preserved on update \u2014 consistent with the create-time semantics in the spec.",
